WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.480
This is not an ordinary bike ride through
town.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.880
And this is not an ordinary bike.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.120
It doesn't have just one back wheel but two
- and they're both tiny.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.160
And forget about the saddle!

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.540
This is not about comfort.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.500
You have to use your whole body to ride a
halfbike and it takes a bit of practice!

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:30.000
"It's a cross between a bike and a skateboard
but when you ride it it's a completely different feeleing.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.600
It's a whole new experience."

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:40.440
Meike Krüger went to Sofia in Bulgaria to
meet the inventors of the halfbike.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.880
So far, all halfbikes are made in this workshop
and sent around the world, mainly to the US.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.880
A halfbike costs 500 euros.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.540
They're easy to fold up which is great for
people who live in big cities.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.880
The designers are originally architects who
love to invent things.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:08.759
"I like to simplify things to an extreme,
so I started to think about a bike, which

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:14.260
is very minimalistic, very compact and very
light.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:22.579
This is how we came up with the idea of the
standing bike.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:30.020
I wanted to create something like a unicycle,
but for everybody.”

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.420
The prototypes consisted of half a bike and
a mini back wheel.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:41.060
Many attempts featuring two mini wheels followed
but they all lacked stability and balance.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.479
The breakthrough came when they started using
two skateboard wheels and a structure made

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:47.080
of aluminium and wood.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.820
Then, the back wheels got bigger and thicker.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:58.340
The designers raised over 70-thousand euros
for their first 100 models on the kickstarter

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.600
crowdfunding platform in 2014.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.579
The year after, they launched another campaign
to raise 900-thousand euros for 2000 bikes.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.410
And since then it's been simply non-stop.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.780
Our reporter first learnt the ropes.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.280
The designers explained that she could only
brake using the back wheels and that there

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.420
were three gears.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.500
They pointed out that the handlebar can't
be twisted.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.180
You have to shift your weight to go around
the corner.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.300
Then it was time to put the theory to the
test.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.400
„The bike will start to turn either direction,
just try to keep it in a straight line.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.860
Try to balance with the handlebar and try
to be as relaxed as possible.”

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.860
At first she wasn't at all relaxed.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.900
She thought she wouldn't make it at all.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.000
It was a bit rough to begin with.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.400
But she got the hang of it after 10 minutes.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:07.960
Although she didn't dare try the tougher courses
- leaving those to more experienced halfbike riders.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.440
She practised a little bit more before venturing
out into the world.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:24.010
Since there are few cycle paths in Sofia,
she preferred to hone her skills in the park

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.720
before confronting the urban jungle.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:31.880
She was able to go straight quite fast but
it took a while to master turns.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.660
Then she decided to see if others were quicker
at learning than she was.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:54.060
It seems that hardly anyone can really ride
a halfbike without a bit of practice!

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:59.060
But those who master it can sometimes ride
two at the same time!

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.320
"It looks so easy but it really isn't.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:11.650
It takes quite a lot of effort and every muscle
is needed.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:16.160
You have to be quite fit to ride a halfbike
but if you are then it's really quite good fun."

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.820
While Meike was having fun and beginning
to master riding the halfbike, the team in

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:30.700
Sofia was already working on new ideas - since
there are many ways of reinventing the wheel.

